WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.998 --> 00:00:15.862
L.A. Detective by Philip Prowse.

3
00:00:20.344 --> 00:00:22.185
My name is Lenny Samuel.

4
00:00:23.206 --> 00:00:24.666
My friends call me Len.

5
00:00:25.687 --> 00:00:26.547
I'm a detective.

6
00:00:27.568 --> 00:00:29.089
I work in Los Angeles.

7
00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:31.850
I'm an L.A. detective.

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.733
Everybody in Los Angeles is busy.

10
00:00:38.015 --> 00:00:39.756
But Len isn't busy.

11
00:00:41.116 --> 00:00:42.677
He's sitting in his office.

12
00:00:43.798 --> 00:00:44.518
He's waiting.

13
00:00:45.919 --> 00:00:47.659
He has no work today.

14
00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.440
Nothing is happening.

15
00:00:52.461 --> 00:00:55.463
Then a man comes into the office.

16
00:00:57.243 --> 00:00:59.124
Len doesn't know him.

17
00:01:00.845 --> 00:01:03.726
The man is short and dark.

18
00:01:05.327 --> 00:01:08.500
He's about 40 years old.

19
00:01:08.857 --> 00:01:10.258
He's wearing a suit.

20
00:01:12.059 --> 00:01:14.300
The man is holding a gun.

21
00:01:15.621 --> 00:01:18.463
The gun is pointing at Len.

22
00:01:20.464 --> 00:01:21.204
"I'm Frank."

23
00:01:22.145 --> 00:01:22.985
"Come with me."

24
00:01:23.906 --> 00:01:26.587
"Mr Blane wants to speak to you."

26
00:01:28.028 --> 00:01:30.110
"I won't go with you, Frank."

27
00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.991
"I don't like Mr Blane."

29
00:01:34.152 --> 00:01:35.913
"I don't want to speak to him."

30
00:01:38.313 --> 00:01:40.415
Frank is a tough man.

31
00:01:41.496 --> 00:01:42.277
He laughs.

32
00:01:43.558 --> 00:01:45.219
He hits Len on the head.

33
00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:47.721
He hits Len hard.

34
00:01:49.002 --> 00:01:50.524
Len's eyes close.

35
00:01:51.805 --> 00:01:53.386
Len falls down.

36
00:01:54.587 --> 00:01:57.550
He falls onto the floor of the office.

37
00:02:04.436 --> 00:02:05.617
Len wakes up.

38
00:02:06.623 --> 00:02:08.084
He opens his eyes.

39
00:02:09.826 --> 00:02:12.068
He's sitting in a big chair.

40
00:02:13.389 --> 00:02:15.190
The room is very warm.

41
00:02:16.672 --> 00:02:18.974
There are lots of plants in the room.

42
00:02:22.156 --> 00:02:22.797
"Where am I?"

43
00:02:23.878 --> 00:02:25.599
"Hello, Mr Samuel."

45
00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.461
"Welcome to my house."

46
00:02:28.122 --> 00:02:32.045
An old man is talking and smiling.

47
00:02:33.366 --> 00:02:34.507
He's Mr Blane.

49
00:02:35.881 --> 00:02:38.400
He's a very rich man.

50
00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:42.126
He's also a very bad man.

51
00:02:44.828 --> 00:02:47.750
"You're going to help me, Mr Samuel."

53
00:02:48.851 --> 00:02:51.153
"You're going to find my daughter."

54
00:02:52.274 --> 00:02:53.615
"Read these letters."

55
00:02:56.077 --> 00:02:57.858
"Carmen is our prisoner."

56
00:02:59.219 --> 00:03:05.800
"We want $100,000. Give us the money."

58
00:03:05.905 --> 00:03:07.285
"Carmen will come home."

59
00:03:08.626 --> 00:03:10.986
"Meet us on Tuesday at 2 p.m."

60
00:03:12.207 --> 00:03:14.067
"Meet us at the bus station."

61
00:03:15.448 --> 00:03:16.308
"The Young Ones."

62
00:03:19.529 --> 00:03:21.209
"Father, help!"

63
00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:23.850
"Please give them the money."

64
00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:25.711
"Carmen."

65
00:03:29.452 --> 00:03:30.892
Carmen is 18.

66
00:03:31.632 --> 00:03:33.553
She has long dark hair.

67
00:03:34.305 --> 00:03:35.686
Her eyes are blue.

68
00:03:36.746 --> 00:03:37.667
She's beautiful.

69
00:03:39.568 --> 00:03:42.109
Mr Blane gives Len a photo.

71
00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:46.531
He says, "I want Carmen back."

72
00:03:47.692 --> 00:03:51.594
"Go to the bus station at two o'clock on Tuesday."

73
00:03:52.774 --> 00:03:55.696
"Frank has the $100,000."

74
00:03:56.656 --> 00:03:57.957
"He's going with you."

75
00:03:59.278 --> 00:04:01.439
"Give the money to the Young Ones."

76
00:04:02.625 --> 00:04:04.086
"Bring Carmen home."

77
00:04:05.486 --> 00:04:08.087
"I'll pay you $1,000."

78
00:04:09.887 --> 00:04:10.648
Len says,

79
00:04:11.728 --> 00:04:13.589
"I don't like you, Blane."

80
00:04:14.549 --> 00:04:15.929
"I don't want your money."

81
00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:18.450
"But Carmen is in trouble."

82
00:04:19.371 --> 00:04:20.091
"She needs help."

83
00:04:21.851 --> 00:04:25.853
"I'll help her."

84
00:04:25.873 --> 00:04:27.993
It's 2 p.m. on Tuesday.

85
00:04:29.254 --> 00:04:32.195
Frank and Len are at the bus station.

86
00:04:33.644 --> 00:04:37.565
Frank has $100,000 in a bag.

87
00:04:39.786 --> 00:04:44.247
Large buses are going in and out of the bus station.

88
00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.488
There are lots of people.

89
00:04:49.189 --> 00:04:51.770
But Len can't see Carmen.

90
00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.011
Frank and Len wait.

91
00:04:57.411 --> 00:04:59.512
Then they see Carmen.

92
00:05:00.852 --> 00:05:02.793
She's standing by a bus.

93
00:05:04.295 --> 00:05:05.917
A young man is with her.

94
00:05:07.218 --> 00:05:10.461
The young man is holding Carmen's arm.

95
00:05:13.063 --> 00:05:16.346
"Hello. Are you Carmen Blane?"

97
00:05:17.687 --> 00:05:18.988
"I'm working for your father."

98
00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:21.310
"Who are you?"

99
00:05:23.172 --> 00:05:24.173
"I'm from the Young Ones."

100
00:05:26.295 --> 00:05:27.055
"Where's the money?"

101
00:05:28.937 --> 00:05:29.798
"Here it is."

102
00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.511
Frank opens the bag.

103
00:05:35.952 --> 00:05:38.193
The young man sees the money.

104
00:05:39.673 --> 00:05:42.955
The young man lets go of Carmen's arm.

105
00:05:44.896 --> 00:05:46.917
Len holds Carmen's arm.

106
00:05:48.258 --> 00:05:51.739
Frank gives the bag of money to the young man.

107
00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:57.022
Suddenly, Carmen bites Len's hand.

108
00:05:58.123 --> 00:06:00.784
Len lets go of Carmen's arm.

109
00:06:05.051 --> 00:06:06.971
The young man hits Frank.

110
00:06:08.091 --> 00:06:09.392
Frank falls down.

111
00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:18.234
Carmen and the young man jump onto the bus.

112
00:06:19.355 --> 00:06:21.475
The door of the bus closes.

113
00:06:22.595 --> 00:06:24.336
The bus drives off.

114
00:06:25.756 --> 00:06:28.237
It's going to San Francisco.

115
00:06:30.177 --> 00:06:32.178
Len can't get on the bus.

116
00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:35.591
He decides to get his car.

117
00:06:37.411 --> 00:06:40.773
Len decides to drive to San Francisco.

118
00:06:46.935 --> 00:06:48.595
Len is in his car.

119
00:06:49.896 --> 00:06:52.417
He's driving to San Francisco.

120
00:06:53.597 --> 00:06:55.518
He's going to find Carmen.

121
00:06:57.799 --> 00:07:00.840
Why is Carmen going to San Francisco?

122
00:07:02.748 --> 00:07:04.329
Who is the young man?

123
00:07:13.096 --> 00:07:13.977
It's Thursday.

124
00:07:15.458 --> 00:07:18.120
Len is in San Francisco.

125
00:07:20.001 --> 00:07:23.144
San Francisco is a big city.

126
00:07:24.725 --> 00:07:26.887
Len can't find Carmen.

127
00:07:28.805 --> 00:07:32.587
Suddenly, Len sees a sign on a building.

128
00:07:34.007 --> 00:07:36.968
The sign says, "The Young Ones."

129
00:07:38.769 --> 00:07:41.610
The building is a school for poor children.

130
00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:45.531
Carmen is playing with the children.

131
00:07:47.172 --> 00:07:48.933
Len stops his car.

132
00:07:50.133 --> 00:07:52.034
He goes to speak to Carmen.

133
00:07:56.335 --> 00:07:57.696
"I don't want to go home."

134
00:07:58.628 --> 00:08:03.250
"I'm happy here. I like working at this school."

136
00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:07.514
"The $100,000 is for the school."

137
00:08:08.935 --> 00:08:10.796
"My father is a bad man."

138
00:08:12.057 --> 00:08:14.619
"These papers show he is a criminal."

139
00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.241
"Take the papers to the police."

140
00:08:19.382 --> 00:08:20.403
"You stay here."

141
00:08:21.544 --> 00:08:22.644
"Nobody will find you."

142
00:08:23.965 --> 00:08:25.706
"I'll take the papers to the police."

143
00:08:27.368 --> 00:08:27.848
"Good luck."

144
00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:36.150
It's Friday.

145
00:08:37.631 --> 00:08:39.792
Len is in Los Angeles.

146
00:08:41.032 --> 00:08:42.633
He's at the police station.

147
00:08:43.873 --> 00:08:47.654
Frank and Blane are at the police station too.

148
00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:52.496
"These papers show that you're a criminal, Blane."

149
00:08:56.037 --> 00:08:56.677
"I'm tired."

150
00:08:57.698 --> 00:08:58.598
"I have no money."

151
00:08:59.739 --> 00:09:01.519
"But I have an exciting job."

152
00:09:02.439 --> 00:09:03.780
"And I like to help people."

153
00:09:04.954 --> 00:09:22.000
"That's why I'm an L.A. detective."